From ab329bc573a6a48a65b3470c4aa68ad7b7bc5731 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eric W. Biederman" <ebiederm@xmission.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Sep 2017 13:06:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 0067/1090] BACKPORT: pids: Move the pgrp and session pid
 pointers from task_struct to signal_struct

To access these fields the code always has to go to group leader so
going to signal struct is no loss and is actually a fundamental simplification.

This saves a little bit of memory by only allocating the pid pointer array
once instead of once for every thread, and even better this removes a
few potential races caused by the fact that group_leader can be changed
by de_thread, while signal_struct can not.

Change-Id: I08d98f7b53db192f5f817195db9119de0e2b4ff1
Signed-off-by: "Eric W. Biederman" <ebiederm@xmission.com>
