From 7398a9cb0c03fb8eeb00ffe9cdc36c268ae6d32d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KP Singh <kpsingh@google.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Mar 2020 20:18:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 0256/1090] UPSTREAM: bpf: Refactor trampoline update code

As we need to introduce a third type of attachment for trampolines, the
flattened signature of arch_prepare_bpf_trampoline gets even more
complicated.

Refactor the prog and count argument to arch_prepare_bpf_trampoline to
use bpf_tramp_progs to simplify the addition and accounting for new
attachment types.

Change-Id: I0e80fce8ba45c49a7c0a9166e27bc60f68aeb140
Signed-off-by: KP Singh <kpsingh@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Alexei Starovoitov <ast@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Andrii Nakryiko <andriin@fb.com>
Acked-by: Daniel Borkmann <daniel@iogearbox.net>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/bpf/20200304191853.1529-2-kpsingh@chromium.org
---
