the new SO_BINDTOIFINDEX to avoid temporarily resolving the device-name
just to look it up in the ioctl again.

Reviewed-by: Tom Gundersen <teg@jklm.no>
Change-Id: Ib7cd56502557a73ab4d155c5cca220567ea7b7fb
Signed-off-by: David Herrmann <dh.herrmann@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>
---
 net/ipv6/ip6_udp_tunnel.c | 15 +++------------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/ipv6/ip6_udp_tunnel.c b/net/ipv6/ip6_udp_tunnel.c
index ad1a9ccd4b44a..25430c991cea3 100644
--- a/net/ipv6/ip6_udp_tunnel.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/ip6_udp_tunnel.c
@@ -32,18 +32,9 @@ int udp_sock_create6(struct net *net, struct udp_port_cfg *cfg,
 			goto error;
 	}
 	if (cfg->bind_ifindex) {
-		struct net_device *dev;
-
-		dev = dev_get_by_index(net, cfg->bind_ifindex);
-		if (!dev) {
-			err = -ENODEV;
-			goto error;
-		}
-
-		err = kernel_setsockopt(sock, SOL_SOCKET, SO_BINDTODEVICE,
-					dev->name, strlen(dev->name) + 1);
-		dev_put(dev);
-
+		err = kernel_setsockopt(sock, SOL_SOCKET, SO_BINDTOIFINDEX,
+					(void *)&cfg->bind_ifindex,
+					sizeof(cfg->bind_ifindex));
 		if (err < 0)
 			goto error;
 	}

From 62f8ccc533060391ec36fd1ff939392478121a35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2020 07:12:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0443/1090] BACKPORT: net: add sock_bindtoindex

Add a helper to directly set the SO_BINDTOIFINDEX sockopt from kernel
space without going through a fake uaccess.

Change-Id: Idb5a895062810cb89b3b7dca8a774b8b2c6161d5
Signed-off-by: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>
Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>
