From 91d8e3c3dd6a8444aa7561b18f6b0ccf2962db43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hou Tao <houtao1@huawei.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Sep 2021 10:33:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 0900/1090] BACKPORT: bpf: Handle return value of
 BPF_PROG_TYPE_STRUCT_OPS prog

[ Upstream commit 356ed64991c6847a0c4f2e8fa3b1133f7a14f1fc ]

Currently if a function ptr in struct_ops has a return value, its
caller will get a random return value from it, because the return
value of related BPF_PROG_TYPE_STRUCT_OPS prog is just dropped.

So adding a new flag BPF_TRAMP_F_RET_FENTRY_RET to tell bpf trampoline
to save and return the return value of struct_ops prog if ret_size of
the function ptr is greater than 0. Also restricting the flag to be
used alone.

