From b7fd861ff543c971bf7474a90d61824e508f9a39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhengchao Shao <shaozhengchao@huawei.com>
Date: Fri, 15 Jul 2022 19:55:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 0930/1090] UPSTREAM: bpf: Don't redirect packets with invalid
 pkt_len

commit fd1894224407c484f652ad456e1ce423e89bb3eb upstream.

Syzbot found an issue [1]: fq_codel_drop() try to drop a flow whitout any
skbs, that is, the flow->head is null.
The root cause, as the [2] says, is because that bpf_prog_test_run_skb()
run a bpf prog which redirects empty skbs.
So we should determine whether the length of the packet modified by bpf
prog or others like bpf_prog_test is valid before forwarding it directly.

LINK: [1] https://syzkaller.appspot.com/bug?id=0b84da80c2917757915afa89f7738a9d16ec96c5
LINK: [2] https://www.spinics.net/lists/netdev/msg777503.html

