From 90dc6a5f3b847d46f13cb154a70afb9dab705831 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micah Morton <mortonm@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 16 Jan 2019 07:46:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 0997/1090] BACKPORT: LSM: add SafeSetID module that gates
 setid calls

SafeSetID gates the setid family of syscalls to restrict UID/GID
transitions from a given UID/GID to only those approved by a
system-wide whitelist. These restrictions also prohibit the given
UIDs/GIDs from obtaining auxiliary privileges associated with
CAP_SET{U/G}ID, such as allowing a user to set up user namespace UID
mappings. For now, only gating the set*uid family of syscalls is
supported, with support for set*gid coming in a future patch set.

Change-Id: I458c47c1d60fee9bf3eed6e0bf559aefd062f77e
Signed-off-by: Micah Morton <mortonm@chromium.org>
Acked-by: Kees Cook <keescook@chromium.org>
Signed-off-by: James Morris <james.morris@microsoft.com>
---
